{{- /*
  Worker Capability Manifest (partial)

  Renders the whole CRUSH_GLOBAL_DATA pin for a Crush worker — the pool
  workers, the difficulty lanes, and triage — from a model and a list of the
  MCP servers that worker actually calls.

  A pin merges OVER the global ~/.config/crush/crush.json, so a server is only
  gone when the pin switches it off BY NAME. Leaving it out of the list keeps
  the global entry, and the global entry is enabled. That is not hypothetical:
  before this partial, every pin named only its model (and, on a lane, its own
  switchboard endpoint), so every worker started with all eleven global
  servers attached. Measured on tars against litellm/Qwen3.8-27B, a pool
  worker's first turn carried 81,309 prompt tokens, 36,007 of them MCP tool
  schemas — and the pool's own history shows it never once called five of
  those servers.

  This is the worker half of what .chezmoitemplates/sweeps/crush.json.tmpl
  does for the scheduled sweeps. It deliberately does NOT touch
  global_context_paths or disabled_tools: a sweep runs one bounded errand from
  a prompt file, while these workers take arbitrary work over a channel, keep
  CRUSH.md as their policy, and have on record used the tools a sweep can
  safely drop.

  $servers must name every MCP server in dot_config/crush/crush.json.tmpl, or
  a new server silently rides into every worker; test/lean-workers.bats checks
  that, the same way test/lean-sweeps.bats checks the sweep half.

  Arguments, as a dict:
    .model     the model id, for both the large and small slots
    .provider  the provider that model is reached through
    .small     optional, a dict overriding the small slot entirely
    .mcp       the MCP servers this worker keeps
    .extra     optional, server name -> definition, merged in after the
               disables (a lane's own switchboard endpoint)

  @joestump 09/16/2026 - Added with the worker capability manifests.
*/ -}}
{{- $servers := list "aws" "aws-knowledge" "cairn" "chrome-devtools" "filesystem" "gitea" "memory" "msgbrowse" "outline" "sequential-thinking" "signal" "switchboard" -}}
{{- range $s := .mcp -}}
{{- if not (has $s $servers) }}{{ fail (printf "worker keeps MCP server %q, which is not in the global crush.json" $s) }}{{ end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $mcp := dict -}}
{{- range $s := $servers -}}
{{- if not (has $s $.mcp) }}{{ $_ := set $mcp $s (dict "disabled" true) }}{{ end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- range $name, $def := (dig "extra" (dict) .) }}{{ $_ := set $mcp $name $def }}{{ end -}}
{{- $large := dict "model" .model "provider" .provider -}}
{{- $small := dig "small" $large . -}}
{{ dict "$schema" "https://charm.land/crush.json" "models" (dict "large" $large "small" $small) "mcp" $mcp | toPrettyJson }}
